+### JFrog CLI publishing, SBOMs and attestations
+
+The Maven and Gradle publish workflows deploy with the JFrog CLI (`jf mvn deploy` / `jf gradle artifactoryPublish`),
+authenticated with GitHub OIDC through `jfrog/setup-jfrog-cli`. The CycloneDX SBOM is deployed with the artifacts
+(Maven: `cyclonedx-maven-plugin`, Gradle: uploaded next to the distribution as `<distribution>-cyclonedx.json`).
+
+The main artifact (`distribution-path`, the distribution zip) gets a GitHub build-provenance attestation and an SBOM
+attestation, whose subject is the zip's path in Artifactory. At the end of the job `setup-jfrog-cli` publishes the
+build-info (with git details) and attaches both attestations to the zip as JFrog evidence. JFrog evidence needs the
+Evidence service; without it the post step only logs a warning.
+
+Callers must grant `id-token: write` and `attestations: write` (and `contents: write` for dependency submission).
+New inputs: `deploy-repo`, `distribution-path` (required), `sbom-path`. `maven-repo-id` is deprecated and ignored.
 
